{"id": "q0409", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 3.01, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1799, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used ?", "transcript": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The Philly Special is a trick play used in American football. It involves the quarterback throwing a short pass to a running back, who then quickly tosses the ball back to the quarterback for a touchdown. The play was famously used by the Philadelphia Eagles during Super Bowl LII in February 2018 to score a game-winning touchdown against the New England Patriots.", "answer_ms": 1788}
{"id": "q0421", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 4.21, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1032, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.", "transcript": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.", "mode": "local", "answer": "Golf irons and drivers are both used in golf, but they serve different purposes on the course. A golf driver is designed for hitting the ball long distances off the tee, especially when starting a hole from the tee box. It has the largest clubhead and the least loft of any club in a set, which allows it to generate maximum distance with a powerful swing. Drivers are typically used for your first shot on a par 3 or par 4 hole, aiming to get the ball as far as possible toward the green.\\n\\nOn the other hand, golf irons are used for shorter shots around the green or when you're not teeing off. They come in various numbers—such as 3-iron, 4-iron, 5-iron, etc.—with each number corresponding to slightly more loft than the one before it. This means irons help you hit the ball higher and with less distance than a driver, making them ideal for approach shots into the green or for playing from rough terrain.\\n\\nIn summary, use a driver when you want maximum distance from the tee, and switch to an iron when you need more control and accuracy for shorter or more challenging shots.", "answer_ms": 6255}
{"id": "q0426", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 2.9, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.11, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "transcript": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The purpose of a shot clock in basketball is to keep the game moving and prevent teams from holding the ball for too long. It ensures that there's continuous action on the court by giving players a limited amount of time to attempt a shot after gaining possession.", "answer_ms": 1198}
